WEBVTT

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:27.020
Eri still hasn't woken up?

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:27.750
Nope.

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:30.190
What did the doctors say?

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:33.360
Light hypersomething.

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:38.170
It sounded like it's because she played The Game too much.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.810
But she'll get well soon, right? That's something.

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:44.690
Yeah...

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:47.420
But they said people usually recover in just a few hours.

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:49.790
Hey, don't worry.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.980
She'll wake up soon.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:01:59.890
Not this one...

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.270
And not this one either.

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:04.940
This is bad.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.890
If I don't have the list, I can't see their data.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:16.900
If Sakuya didn't get PK'd by them, then it's okay.

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:21.280
I wonder what the real Sakuya is like.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:22.890
I'd really like to meet her.

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:29.420
No way... She wasn't put to sleep, right?

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:40.660
The cat guy fell down there, then that blackness spread.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:45.190
So either there's something down there...

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:47.430
Or the cat guy did something.

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:50.340
Let's check it out.

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:58.370
Please don't use telecommunication devices in the hospital!

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:00.990
Yeah...

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:04.450
Thank you very much.

00:03:05.210 --> 00:03:06.300
How was it?

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:10.190
My hands are still a bit numb, but they said I'll be all right.

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:12.890
And they told me I shouldn't play The Game for a while.

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:17.590
I see. Anyway... Let's go?

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:21.550
Huh, she's not here...

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:23.310
Did they let her out already?

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:27.580
Excuse me! The girl who was sleeping here...

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:30.560
Ah, her? She was transported to another hospital this morning.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:38.590
Just as I thought.

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:38.980
Huh?

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:42.280
Look here. They're funded by a private company.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:51.890
I heard a rumor that players who fall unconscious while in The World get moved into private hospitals.

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:55.500
You just know the owner's hiding something.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:56.950
Hiding something?

00:03:56.950 --> 00:04:00.650
Yeah. The connection between The World and these coma victims.

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:06.060
You said that when you touched Eri, you were repelled, right?

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:10.730
Didn't you touch her with this hand?

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:18.020
There is an urban legend about The World...

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:22.280
It says that the soul of the player gets sucked in, and while they're unconscious in the real world,

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:26.460
their character is still logged into The Game, walking around.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:28.570
No way! Don't joke about such things!

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:29.660
That's just identity theft, isn't it?

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:31.380
Dunno.

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:33.750
But this has to be more than just a coincidence.

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:36.750
And about the changing hospitals!

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:41.570
The equipment at the previous hospital was way better,

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:44.730
and yet she was moved to a hospital out of town! That doesn't make sense!

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:46.060
It must be that the owner is-

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:47.450
I don't get it!

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:51.360
I want to do something to help Eri...

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:55.440
But telling me these occult stories...

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:57.870
I don't get it!

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:04.450
A net game?

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:07.330
An awesome net game!

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:09.240
You should try it too, Eri!

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:12.650
No way! It sounds so creepy!

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:13.950
Huh?

00:05:16.930 --> 00:05:17.750
Good evening!

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:22.700
Oh! So you chose the Black Rose type!

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:24.390
Our new teammate!

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:26.830
And that is?

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:29.190
Ah, that's Tobias.

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:32.600
We became friends when I first joined The World.

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:34.640
Nice to meet you.

00:05:38.510 --> 00:05:40.820
Sakuya, make use of your abilities!

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:43.570
The knockback will throw you back there, so use ranged attacks!

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:45.730
I didn't get a word of that!

00:05:45.730 --> 00:05:46.850
Sakuya, behind you!

00:05:46.850 --> 00:05:47.510
Fast!

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:51.140
Hey, wha-

00:05:56.990 --> 00:05:58.070
Asumi?

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:06.000
Hey, Iori...

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:10.930
Is Eri in The World?

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:13.430
Dunno.

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:15.440
But I think it'd be better if she wasn't.

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:20.410
If she was stuck there...

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:21.650
I'd really have

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:24.470
no idea how to help her.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.230
Should I walk you home?

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:33.840
I'm fine. And sorry...

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:39.820
Hey, can I stop by your place after school tomorrow?

00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:40.950
Huh?

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:43.140
That story you told me...

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:45.510
I really don't want to believe it.

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:46.800
But it's scary.

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:48.300
And...

00:06:48.690 --> 00:06:52.050
I want to do everything I can.

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:58.060
We're the only ones that know what happened before Eri collapsed.

00:06:58.520 --> 00:06:59.800
Hey, boss!

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:03.120
I brought you that list you asked for.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:06.160
The content is pretty much the same as last time.

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:08.350
Users who have microchip implants.

00:07:08.350 --> 00:07:13.320
Also, it has some new users not in the previous one.

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:18.030
But you'll have to crack those 200 000 passwords yourself.

00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:20.330
It'd take way too long for me.

00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:21.570
Obliged.

00:07:22.030 --> 00:07:24.080
May I ask what you're gonna use it for?

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:25.010
Secret.

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:28.520
Hey now, just don't be reckless with it!

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:30.470
I don't want to get involved in anything.

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:31.770
Thanks for the advice.

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:42.940
The password cracks are nearly finished.

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:46.170
I guess this should be fine.

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:48.510
It won't matter if someone sees them, either.

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:53.360
Let's check the PK'd guys too.

00:07:57.040 --> 00:08:00.080
I thought we'd be doing it more like detectives.

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:02.800
That's right, Watson-kun.

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:06.010
Sakuya, your right hand...

00:08:07.470 --> 00:08:08.090
Huh?

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:10.180
What's this?

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:14.590
As I thought. The numbness in your hand is somehow related to this.

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:16.520
Let's look into it later.

00:08:17.570 --> 00:08:20.060
Okay, let's go!

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:21.180
First, jump!

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:26.290
Sakuya, here I go!

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:34.110
This won't work, huh?

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:40.300
So it's not a warp zone.

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:43.720
So that cat PC had something to do with it.

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:10.010
What's this?

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:12.680
A scroll? Where did you pick it up?

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:14.060
Dunno...

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:18.780
What... What's this?!

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:22.110
Personal data on someone?

00:09:24.850 --> 00:09:26.270
Iori, there!

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:28.930
That's...

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:33.410
What the hell's going on here?

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:35.660
Eri...

00:09:38.560 --> 00:09:45.440
Masaya Asanuma, 059-18fd-0bc2.

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:46.030
Yep.

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:54.820
Kouichi Matsubara, 046-7d9a-bc1a.

00:09:55.270 --> 00:09:55.980
Yep.

00:09:55.980 --> 00:10:02.360
Kana Sugimoto, 098-da12-bdcc

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:04.270
Hey...

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:05.080
Huh?

00:10:05.430 --> 00:10:08.720
Do you think they're all comatose?

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:11.480
That's right. Let's check it out.

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:12.710
What are you going to do?

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:13.960
I'll call them, of course.

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:17.880
Wow, they are all hospitalized!?

00:10:18.730 --> 00:10:22.450
And these are all CC Company hospitals!

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:25.580
I wouldn't have thought it was this serious.

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:28.520
Will it be all right?

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:29.600
What?

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:34.030
But aren't we getting too deeply involved in this?

00:10:34.030 --> 00:10:35.300
We should call the poli-

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:39.390
Caller unavailable.

00:10:42.690 --> 00:10:43.870
So persistent.

00:10:49.230 --> 00:10:52.260
It's probably one of the people I called earlier.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:58.910
No way.

00:10:58.910 --> 00:11:00.360
Hello, Ikuta speaking.

00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:02.720
Wait a second.

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:05.140
Sis, call for you!

00:11:06.020 --> 00:11:07.850
That idiot.

00:11:09.340 --> 00:11:11.310
It's me.

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:13.000
Ikuta Iori, right?

00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:15.360
And who would you be?

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:20.000
The ones you called earlier are The Sleepers.

00:11:20.350 --> 00:11:24.700
How did you find them all in the week since Etou Eri fell asleep?

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:29.390
Who are you? How do you know about Eri?

00:11:29.390 --> 00:11:31.210
Investigating this is part of my job.

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:33.440
It's not my intent to hurt anyone.

00:11:33.450 --> 00:11:35.610
I'm going to send you two tickets,

00:11:35.610 --> 00:11:38.210
please use them to come to Tokyo with your friend.

00:11:39.020 --> 00:11:42.220
I will email you the place and time of our meeting.

00:11:49.070 --> 00:11:51.390
Hey, what's going on here?

00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:07.050
Who made this?

00:12:07.050 --> 00:12:08.040
Sakuya!

00:12:15.990 --> 00:12:17.250
Hermit!

00:12:17.690 --> 00:12:19.230
So you're all right!

00:12:19.780 --> 00:12:21.260
I've been looking for you!

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:23.430
Ah... Sorry.

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:25.510
Is something wrong?

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:27.510
Unconscious?

00:12:27.510 --> 00:12:33.020
Yeah... My friend who got PK'd when we last met... Mary.

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:36.180
And there's even more.

00:12:36.180 --> 00:12:38.810
We received a call from someone strange.

00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:43.080
Well, I need to get some sleep.

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:46.640
Will you be online tomorrow, too?

00:12:46.670 --> 00:12:49.030
Sorry, I've got plans.

00:12:50.470 --> 00:12:51.360
See you!

00:12:59.050 --> 00:13:01.050
We don't have any other leads!

00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:03.190
We've no choice but to go!

00:13:03.190 --> 00:13:07.710
I'm just saying that we should be more careful.

00:13:07.710 --> 00:13:09.390
It's fine if you're not coming.

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:11.370
I'll go alone.

00:13:11.890 --> 00:13:12.640
Idiot!

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:14.810
When did I say I'm not going?

00:13:27.480 --> 00:13:30.120
Is there a festival going on?

00:13:33.840 --> 00:13:35.300
This way. Let's go.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:40.380
That's the UN building!

00:13:40.740 --> 00:13:43.440
Just an investigator, my ass.

00:13:54.590 --> 00:13:54.990
Yes?

00:13:55.550 --> 00:13:56.390
Log in please.

00:14:00.790 --> 00:14:02.140
Open the door.

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:14.630
Iori!

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:25.170
Those people are players that have fallen unconscious because of a problem within The World.

00:14:29.730 --> 00:14:32.110
If you know that much, then w-

00:14:33.090 --> 00:14:40.490
Our current knowledge is insufficient to determine any connections between The Sleepers and The Game.

00:14:47.730 --> 00:14:49.700
Welcome to my stronghold.

00:14:50.220 --> 00:14:51.400
You're...

00:14:51.400 --> 00:14:53.840
I apologize for all the trouble.

00:14:53.840 --> 00:14:55.490
No, it's my-

00:14:56.330 --> 00:15:00.060
Did you call us here to show us that?

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:02.210
Don't be so blunt.

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:07.210
The World is responsible for the sudden comas.

00:15:07.990 --> 00:15:11.120
It also contains the path for returning to consciousness.

00:15:11.120 --> 00:15:14.720
I hope you're not just telling us what we want to hear.

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:16.640
This is no lie.

00:15:17.090 --> 00:15:21.710
I was a Sleeper five years ago.

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:27.620
In 2017, there was a powerful force operating behind the scenes.

00:15:27.620 --> 00:15:31.190
Without getting rid of that, the people were unable to regain consciousness.

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:33.900
But you're back, aren't you?

00:15:33.900 --> 00:15:37.040
Yeah, but some of us didn't make it.

00:15:37.410 --> 00:15:38.370
Now tell me,

00:15:38.690 --> 00:15:43.160
how did you find The Sleepers?

00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:44.430
In the net slum.

00:15:45.070 --> 00:15:48.770
I was serious. We need to collaborate.

00:15:48.770 --> 00:15:51.470
How could we be serious with someone that looks like a child?

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:52.300
If you want to collaborate,

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:55.100
why don't you show yourself?

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:59.390
I thought it would be easier this way, but well...

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:01.380
Take off your FMD.

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:06.400
Nice to meet you.

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:12.030
Just to clear things up,

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:15.160
That character isn't my preference.

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:19.650
It's just convenient when looking for missing people.

00:16:19.650 --> 00:16:20.760
I see.

00:16:20.760 --> 00:16:22.460
Now, can we talk?

00:16:23.490 --> 00:16:27.040
You haven't told us anything, yet.

00:16:28.430 --> 00:16:30.740
If I do, will you tell me
what I want to know?

00:16:31.230 --> 00:16:33.050
If I believe what you say...

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:38.800
And what if I tell you the truth, but you don't believe me?

00:16:38.800 --> 00:16:39.540
That's...

00:16:39.540 --> 00:16:41.940
If it's true, I'll believe you.

00:16:41.960 --> 00:16:42.840
Hey!

00:16:43.420 --> 00:16:45.990
It was suspicious when we got the email,

00:16:45.990 --> 00:16:48.090
but we're here, aren't we?

00:16:48.100 --> 00:16:49.020
Let's listen to what she has to say.

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:57.610
Ever since the CC Company released The World, there was a grave problem with the game.

00:16:57.610 --> 00:17:02.840
It was used in many forms, and is based on the dream of a certain researcher.

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:05.770
The dream to make all of humankind fall unconscious,

00:17:05.770 --> 00:17:09.210
and free people from racism.

00:17:09.860 --> 00:17:13.210
That dream backfired on him and got out of control.

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:19.640
But thanks to the fire at the CC Company, that researcher himself became a Sleeper,

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:22.450
and for a while the curtains closed on this case.

00:17:23.300 --> 00:17:27.680
But there is an organization that continued his research.

00:17:28.030 --> 00:17:31.320
Their purpose is to control the states of consciousness.

00:17:32.850 --> 00:17:38.020
But they've already begun experimenting on people, and some of the subjects may never come back.

00:17:38.020 --> 00:17:40.850
People that no one would miss.

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:46.370
This is surprising.

00:17:46.670 --> 00:17:49.290
This is a log of the crimes, isn't it?

00:17:50.310 --> 00:17:51.530
Where did you get this?

00:17:52.210 --> 00:17:53.580
Well...

00:17:53.580 --> 00:17:55.860
I usually don't look when I pick things up, so...

00:17:55.860 --> 00:17:56.960
I see.

00:17:56.960 --> 00:18:00.390
For now, please let me have this list.

00:18:01.020 --> 00:18:06.340
By analyzing its data, we may be able to identify its programmer.

00:18:06.860 --> 00:18:11.110
Leave the rest to us. And stop playing The World.

00:18:11.990 --> 00:18:14.350
I will contact you through this man.

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:17.970
Stop playing? But we...

00:18:17.970 --> 00:18:20.950
You might be close to the culprit!

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:24.960
There's a chance you're being targeted! Be careful.

00:18:25.960 --> 00:18:29.460
I feel like I've been smacked over the head with a club.

00:18:30.110 --> 00:18:34.320
Things like this are completely out of our league.

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:36.590
It'll be fine!

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:40.340
You know a lot of things that I have no idea about!

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:42.170
Coming from you, that isn't saying much...

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:45.780
I'm only joking.

00:18:46.130 --> 00:18:46.940
Thank you.

00:18:48.920 --> 00:18:51.230
This is astonishing.

00:18:51.750 --> 00:18:55.610
I want to cut them from the system and release them.

00:18:56.770 --> 00:18:59.220
Do you know what this is?

00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:00.230
No idea.

00:19:00.890 --> 00:19:01.490
Look.

00:19:02.150 --> 00:19:06.490
This one is made of 14 billion q-bits.

00:19:07.110 --> 00:19:11.550
It's probably manipulating the activity of every brain synapse.

00:19:12.060 --> 00:19:14.750
It's a quantum computer.

00:19:15.180 --> 00:19:16.200
Can we free them?

00:19:16.200 --> 00:19:19.830
Sure. If we destroy it, the ones trapped in it should be freed.

00:19:19.830 --> 00:19:23.050
But since their brain is a part of it, they could just die, instead...

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:26.900
But don't worry, I'll disconnect them nicely.

00:19:26.900 --> 00:19:28.470
I can't wait.

00:19:29.970 --> 00:19:32.590
How is your friend?

00:19:32.590 --> 00:19:34.390
The same.

00:19:34.390 --> 00:19:35.510
I see...

00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:38.850
Our search yielded quite a few results.

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:40.530
First things first.

00:19:41.540 --> 00:19:42.880
This list is

00:19:42.880 --> 00:19:46.020
a database of players' haplotypes.

00:19:46.020 --> 00:19:47.620
Haplotype?

00:19:47.840 --> 00:19:51.260
To put it simply, a combination of genes.

00:19:51.260 --> 00:19:54.580
It seems that the creator of the list

00:19:54.580 --> 00:19:57.300
was looking for a donor for someone's treatment using The World.

00:19:57.980 --> 00:20:00.820
But why The World?

00:20:01.330 --> 00:20:05.270
It's easy to exploit security weaknesses.

00:20:05.270 --> 00:20:08.440
Highly secret information, like haplotypes,

00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:11.230
is always protected by very strong security.

00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:14.260
But if they use a social security number...

00:20:14.260 --> 00:20:17.820
Wait! Countries are supposed to manage real-world ID's.

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:21.820
Another thing, is it even possible to extract real-world data from the game?

00:20:22.670 --> 00:20:24.710
Let me show you.

00:20:27.680 --> 00:20:28.410
The list!

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:33.330
As for the culprit, we found the ID of the treatment recipient.

00:20:33.910 --> 00:20:37.140
But he's in America, so we couldn't get any further.

00:20:37.140 --> 00:20:38.570
So that's why you're planning to go to America?

00:20:39.350 --> 00:20:43.330
The name of the recipient is Touha Tanagami, a Japanese national.

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:47.590
He was hospitalized in San Francisco until 2015.

00:20:47.590 --> 00:20:48.600
Was?

00:20:49.120 --> 00:20:51.330
So they let him out?

00:20:51.330 --> 00:20:52.230
No.

00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:53.720
He died.

00:20:53.720 --> 00:20:55.230
In 2015.

00:20:56.350 --> 00:20:59.560
So they looked for a donor for a dead person?

00:20:59.560 --> 00:21:01.230
It seems so.

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:04.960
The point is, for the sake of that recipient,

00:21:04.970 --> 00:21:08.270
the culprit was scheming in The World.

00:21:09.400 --> 00:21:10.800
Died...

00:21:10.800 --> 00:21:12.210
Seven years ago...

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:18.460
He forcibly extracted personal information from the holder of the ID,

00:21:18.460 --> 00:21:20.580
which resulted in the victim falling unconscious.

00:21:21.940 --> 00:21:24.470
Now Sakuya, tell us your password.

00:21:26.440 --> 00:21:28.780
What are you doing? I was almost there!

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:32.430
It was all in vain!

00:21:34.780 --> 00:21:36.770
He's already dead!

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:38.360
What are you talking about?

00:21:46.210 --> 00:21:48.950
If you have an FMD and some skills,

00:21:49.320 --> 00:21:52.450
this is all that it takes to crack an implant's security.

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:53.670
No way!

00:21:53.670 --> 00:21:56.710
The implant holds all our private data!

00:21:56.710 --> 00:21:59.430
You have just seen the truth.

00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:01.960
What?

00:22:02.760 --> 00:22:03.740
A match?

00:22:08.520 --> 00:22:09.300
What?

00:22:42.390 --> 00:22:43.110
Master!

00:22:44.250 --> 00:22:49.260
Dear players! This area will soon be undergoing server maintenance. Please log out immediately.

00:22:49.260 --> 00:22:50.130
This...

00:22:50.130 --> 00:22:54.320
Dear players! This area will soon be undergoing server maintenance. Please log out immediately.

00:23:00.980 --> 00:23:02.630
It's eating something!

00:23:02.630 --> 00:23:04.100
You're kidding me.

00:23:04.100 --> 00:23:06.650
Master, this area is being hacked.

00:23:06.650 --> 00:23:08.060
Can you neutralize it?

00:23:08.060 --> 00:23:08.780
I'll try.

00:23:22.870 --> 00:23:23.610
Eri!

00:23:23.610 --> 00:23:24.960
What? Wait!

00:23:25.260 --> 00:23:26.080
Eri!

00:23:27.550 --> 00:23:28.720
Ouch!

00:23:29.140 --> 00:23:29.830
It hurts?

00:23:29.830 --> 00:23:31.270
Log out!

00:23:31.270 --> 00:23:33.120
This place is not Mac Anu anymore!

00:23:42.360 --> 00:23:43.370
Damn, it doesn't work!

00:23:43.370 --> 00:23:45.050
What did you do to Eri?

00:23:45.050 --> 00:23:46.500
Data Drain!

00:23:46.500 --> 00:23:48.140
But it regenerates too fast!

00:23:50.620 --> 00:23:51.710
This is bad.

00:23:51.710 --> 00:23:53.160
We've got to log off right now!

00:23:53.430 --> 00:23:56.340
If we're PK'd here, we'll turn into Sleepers!

00:23:56.730 --> 00:23:58.740
No! I'm not going home without Eri!

00:23:58.740 --> 00:23:59.850
How...?

00:24:00.700 --> 00:24:01.760
Sakuya!

00:24:02.960 --> 00:24:05.710
I can't let this happen.

00:24:14.640 --> 00:24:16.400
Eri!

00:24:28.240 --> 00:24:33.000
With a feverish heat
Ukareta netsu no naka ni

00:24:33.000 --> 00:24:38.240
Sleeping more in the day than ever before
Ikudo to sugiru hi no nemuri

00:24:38.240 --> 00:24:48.150
When i woke up what did i see to make my heart dance?
Mezameta toki ni mune wa nani wo mite odoru no ka

00:24:48.150 --> 00:24:56.990
Where did i promise to return to?
Doko he modoru to yakusoku shita no?

00:24:56.990 --> 00:25:09.870
We can't return to the ever-repeating old memories
Kurikaeshita tooi kioku ni wa kaerenai

00:25:09.870 --> 00:25:17.490
Please, that moment of happiness
Negai yo, hitotoki no yorokobi ni

00:25:17.490 --> 00:25:20.320
Should last forever
Towa wo egaite

00:25:20.320 --> 00:25:29.720
If those sunk in sorrow cried that there's no help,
Sukui wa nai to shizumi yuku mono ga naita nara

00:25:29.720 --> 00:25:41.410
Remember the warmth that wasn't faked
Mayakasi ja nai nukumori wo omoidashite

00:25:52.480 --> 00:25:53.390
Conquest.

00:25:53.390 --> 00:25:54.320
Solitude.

00:25:54.320 --> 00:25:54.980
Dark clouds.

00:25:54.980 --> 00:25:55.900
Selection.

00:25:55.900 --> 00:25:57.140
Freezing.

00:25:57.140 --> 00:25:58.150
Berserk.

00:25:58.150 --> 00:25:58.960
Cause and effect

00:25:58.960 --> 00:25:59.990
Fainting.

00:25:59.990 --> 00:26:00.970
Donor.

00:26:00.970 --> 00:26:02.260
Recipient.

00:26:02.300 --> 00:26:03.310
Despair.

00:26:03.310 --> 00:26:04.310
Rebirth.

00:26:04.310 --> 00:26:06.500
The end.

00:26:06.500 --> 00:26:09.540
.hack//Quantum. Please watch the next one too.
